  "description": "A flow-controlled pump braking a gravity line, its setpoint over its minimum speed beyond x_mono, so that the head at its setpoint falls with speed below s_lo: the line needs a head between the lowest head on the stable bracket and the head at minimum speed. Verifies that the pump stays active (rule A2 on F(s_lo, Q_set)) with the speed root on [s_lo, s_max], in closed form for a straight curve, and PUMP_OUTSIDE_CURVE at that speed.",
  "source": "closed-form: tests/reference/derivations_pump_control.py::pump_flow_control_stable_bracket (flow control (proposal vfd-pump-modes.md 2.4, 4.5): active Q = Q_set with s* from s*^2 H0(Q_set/s*) = EGL_d - EGL_s; at a limit the fixed-speed pump at s_max or s_min; pump curve: scipy PchipInterpolator, linear end-slope extension, affinity laws; R2 level set so that H(Q_set) = -2 m; s_lo = Q_set/x_mono, x_mono = 2a/b (proposal 4.3); s* = [bQ + sqrt(b^2 Q^2 + 4aH)]/(2a), the root on [s_lo, s_max]; line fittings: fluids bend_rounded_Crane(Di, 90, bend_diameters=1.5), entrance_sharp(method='Crane'), exit_normal())",
